1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,660
[Disclaimer: This series is created
solely for entertainment purposes.

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:03,330
All individuals, behaviors, places,
and events depicted are entirely fictional,

3
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:05,000
with no intention to represent or reference any
organizations, departments, occupations, or individuals]

4
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:06,440
I'll make things right

5
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,460
in three months.

6
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:11,240
Don't you realize our relationship
was never normal to begin with?

7
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:13,640
But we still have three months to
get back to how it used to be.

8
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,460
So it's really you, Sun.

9
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:17,380
Back then, you said Sun's father

10
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:19,100
took her overseas.

11
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:20,580
She lost her memories,

12
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:21,680
so her father took the opportunity

13
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:23,460
to start her life anew over there.

14
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:25,000
I think Sun got her memories back.

15
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:30,440
Our brains are complex.

16
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:32,720
Chris remembers you,

17
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:34,560
but she still had an affair.

18
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:36,080
Perhaps...

19
00:00:36,460 --> 00:00:38,240
her memories alone aren't enough.

20
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:46,600
You first have to know

21
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,480
what Chris is planning to do.

22
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:52,920
If I do, Chris will be mine again, right?

23
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:01,480
Nice flowers.

24
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:03,840
Who gave them to you?

25
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:05,040
My friend.

26
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:06,960
Sun...

27
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:08,240
Who is that?

28
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,700
How did you get in here?

29
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:15,120
And who is Sun?

30
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,200
A friend who helped me come up
with the flower dishes.

31
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:53,320
Whoever dares to take
Chris away from me

32
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:55,480
will die.

33
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:20,240
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

34
00:02:20,260 --> 00:02:25,360
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

35
00:02:25,380 --> 00:02:29,260
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

36
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:35,480
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

37
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:45,220
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

38
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:50,280
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

39
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:54,580
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

40
00:02:54,600 --> 00:03:03,240
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

41
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:12,400
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

42
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:54,200
If you start,

43
00:03:54,220 --> 00:03:55,400
I won't stop you.

44
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:58,680
No, no, no, no.

45
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:00,840
I...

46
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:02,600
I didn't mean to start it.

47
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:04,320
I just...

48
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:08,000
I just saw you were a bit exposed,
so I tried to cover you up.

49
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:15,720
I don't like people who make up excuses.

50
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:17,880
If you want to do it, just say so.

51
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:24,480
Oh?!

52
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:26,160
Sorry.

53
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:29,000
Are you hurt?

54
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:30,880
I was just teasing you.

55
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:45,360
That's "Kiiro",

56
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:47,400
the one I've told you about.

57
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:50,720
She really is yellow.

58
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:52,360
Cute.

59
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:57,700
I'm hungry.

60
00:04:57,720 --> 00:04:59,720
I want the hot cocoa
you make on rainy days.

61
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,320
It's not raining today,

62
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,120
but I'll make it just for you.

63
00:05:59,420 --> 00:06:00,480
What are you looking for?

64
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:06,280
I just wanted to tell you
that I ran out of cocoa,

65
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:09,600
but it seems like you
didn't really want any.

66
00:06:26,820 --> 00:06:28,360
I locked my drawers.

67
00:06:28,660 --> 00:06:29,800
What do you want to know?

68
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:33,560
I'm sorry.

69
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:40,280
If you want to know something,

70
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:41,920
just ask.

71
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:44,600
You didn't have to lie to me.

72
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:49,880
And are you lying to me, Sun?

73
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:55,720
I don't think it's true that
we've never known each other before.

74
00:06:57,840 --> 00:06:58,960
"Kiiro."

75
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:00,760
It's not a very common name.

76
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:04,960
So why do my fish and your dog
have the same name?

77
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:09,960
It's not a coincidence, right?

78
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:15,800
Did you know me before this?

79
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:18,280
Were we...

80
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:21,440
more than just acquaintances?

81
00:07:25,180 --> 00:07:27,040
If we actually used to know each other,

82
00:07:29,780 --> 00:07:31,200
would anything change?

83
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:36,160
Would you think of me differently?

84
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:38,960
Would you still like me?

85
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:45,080
If you're with me right now,

86
00:07:48,540 --> 00:07:50,540
it's better if we don't know each other.

87
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:56,280
I'm sorry.

88
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:00,600
I just want to know the truth.

89
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:05,960
Who we are right now

90
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,200
is the truth.

91
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:20,620
It's so frustrating, Doc.

92
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:22,720
I don't know what's real anymore.

93
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:26,480
Didn't you say you could find
the answers yourself?

94
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:31,680
Then I'm probably all talk, like you said.

95
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:33,660
Right now, I just want to fall asleep,

96
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:35,840
then wake up remembering everything.

97
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:40,620
Do you really want to
remember everything again?

98
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:46,020
Don't you remember...

99
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:47,720
that the reason you're still alive

100
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:49,680
is that you ran from the truth?

101
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:51,560
Can you stop sleeping somewhere else?

102
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:55,040
I feel like I'm going to lose you.

103
00:09:55,660 --> 00:09:57,160
Nadear, but we broke up...

104
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:58,400
I know...

105
00:09:58,860 --> 00:10:00,960
But you said you'll give
me three months.

106
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:04,440
You can go anywhere
or talk to anyone.

107
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:06,320
I won't complain.

108
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:08,520
But please,

109
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:10,560
come back and sleep at home.

110
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,360
Don't take away any more
of my time with you.

111
00:10:18,120 --> 00:10:19,200
Okay...

112
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:20,800
I'll try.

113
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:24,160
Very good.

114
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:28,200
Thank you.

115
00:10:32,740 --> 00:10:35,440
Mm... I bought you some fresh roses.

116
00:10:35,980 --> 00:10:37,980
I already put them in the vase,

117
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:40,260
since the dried-up roses in your room

118
00:10:40,280 --> 00:10:42,000
had all fallen over.

119
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:16,560
She probably didn't want to hurt you.

120
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:18,280
"The truth"

121
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:19,920
doesn't necessarily mean
it'll be a good thing.

122
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:23,960
And how is lying any better?

123
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:26,440
Then... if you know
the truth will hurt,

124
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:28,900
are you still willing to find out?

125
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:32,760
Chris...

126
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:35,960
Chris...

127
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:39,400
Chris!

128
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:41,640
Chris!

129
00:11:46,940 --> 00:11:48,120
Chris...

130
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:51,040
Chris.

131
00:11:53,660 --> 00:11:54,600
Chris!

132
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:11,480
Chris.

133
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:16,120
This one isn't an offering.

134
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,960
I want to give it to you.

135
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:45,080
Chris?!

136
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:48,120
Chris?!

137
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:51,360
Did you have a nightmare?

138
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:53,260
What was it about?

139
00:13:04,580 --> 00:13:07,340
[Third Person]

140
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:12,340
[Third Person]

141
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:15,820
Those doors...

142
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:18,900
will lead you to the past

143
00:13:19,140 --> 00:13:20,740
that caused you pain.

144
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:24,300
Is that why they are locked?

145
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:26,620
It's your body's defense mechanism.

146
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,580
What if I want to go in?

147
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,500
I'll guide you there.

148
00:13:37,060 --> 00:13:38,940
But are you sure...

149
00:13:39,260 --> 00:13:41,600
you want to face those
painful memories?

150
00:14:04,060 --> 00:14:06,380
The reason you were in shock,
lost your memories,

151
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:09,180
and couldn't talk for a year

152
00:14:10,040 --> 00:14:13,060
was because you saw your
parents pass away in the accident.

153
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:41,820
I'm not sure if I'm ready to
remember everything.

154
00:14:42,300 --> 00:14:44,300
If it's too much for you,

155
00:14:45,180 --> 00:14:47,440
you don't have to put yourself through it.

156
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:54,020
Just let the past be the past.

157
00:14:55,580 --> 00:14:58,300
Some memories are better forgotten.

158
00:15:15,340 --> 00:15:16,740
I already told you.

159
00:15:17,060 --> 00:15:19,620
You can talk to anyone or do anything.

160
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:23,980
I won't stop you from making
those flower dishes anymore.

161
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:25,700
You can go ahead with the promotions.

162
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:29,500
I only ask you one thing:

163
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:32,500
come back and sleep at our house.

164
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:47,940
Hello,

165
00:15:48,380 --> 00:15:50,020
are you free tonight?

166
00:16:00,420 --> 00:16:01,600
Judging by that look,

167
00:16:01,620 --> 00:16:03,380
you were turned down again, weren't you?

168
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:06,100
You know too much.

169
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:08,900
Chris said she's going home,

170
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:11,340
so she can't sleep with me.

171
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:13,980
You already asked her to sleep with you,

172
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:16,340
so why didn't you just tell her
the truth at this point?

173
00:16:19,780 --> 00:16:21,340
I'll tell her after we've done
more than sleep together.

174
00:16:22,620 --> 00:16:23,460
Why?

175
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:28,560
Chris has told me...

176
00:16:28,580 --> 00:16:30,100
she had a trauma

177
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:31,480
that made her scared of any physical touch.

178
00:16:32,940 --> 00:16:34,100
It was because of me.

179
00:16:36,580 --> 00:16:38,540
If Chris did more than sleep with you,

180
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:40,140
would that mean...

181
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:42,580
she got over her trauma?

182
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:45,440
I don't know.

183
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:47,860
But at least,

184
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:50,500
I'll be able to forgive myself a little more.

185
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:54,940
[Third Person
Bar - Bistro]

186
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:08,380
[Expenses]

187
00:17:10,180 --> 00:17:11,060
[Total expenses]

188
00:17:30,740 --> 00:17:31,460
Nadear,

189
00:17:32,480 --> 00:17:33,940
have you ever checked
our restaurant's accounts?

190
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,420
Are you still at the restaurant?

191
00:17:36,420 --> 00:17:38,080
I just got over a migraine.

192
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:39,880
I want to know who is in charge
of ordering the supplies,

193
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:42,440
and who is managing
our expenses and income.

194
00:17:42,460 --> 00:17:44,240
Can we discuss this when we're at home?

195
00:17:44,260 --> 00:17:44,980
Nadear,

196
00:17:45,620 --> 00:17:46,740
I'm serious.

197
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:49,680
I saw that the expenses were unusually high,

198
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:51,200
so I went back to check.

199
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:53,880
They gradually increased

200
00:17:53,900 --> 00:17:56,140
over the past three years
before I got out of the hospital.

201
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:58,660
Normally, Nan is in charge of our stock

202
00:17:58,680 --> 00:17:59,660
and accounting.

203
00:18:00,460 --> 00:18:01,940
I did keep an eye on it from time to time.

204
00:18:02,420 --> 00:18:04,540
But our restaurant has more customers.

205
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:06,200
When we make more income,

206
00:18:06,220 --> 00:18:08,660
it's normal for our expenses to be higher too.

207
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:10,980
Nadear, this is very unusual.

208
00:18:11,660 --> 00:18:13,280
The prices we paid

209
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:15,340
are a lot higher than the market price.

210
00:18:15,660 --> 00:18:17,740
I don't think Nan is stealing from us,

211
00:18:18,540 --> 00:18:20,700
but when I see these numbers, it's...

212
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:23,420
You have to take it slow

213
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:25,160
with Nan.

214
00:18:25,940 --> 00:18:27,380
Let me check it out.

215
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:30,300
Don't tell Nan yet.

216
00:18:30,820 --> 00:18:32,040
Let me handle it.

217
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:42,220
That's dangerous.

218
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:46,780
Did I surprise you?

219
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:51,860
One of the waiters said...

220
00:18:52,700 --> 00:18:54,100
you've been in here for a while,

221
00:18:55,020 --> 00:18:56,140
so I came to check on you.

222
00:18:57,380 --> 00:18:58,940
Is there anything I can help you with?

223
00:19:00,060 --> 00:19:00,940
So? Chris?

224
00:19:02,220 --> 00:19:03,940
Is there anything you'd like to ask me?

225
00:19:05,180 --> 00:19:07,140
Nan, holding a knife like that is dangerous.

226
00:19:08,460 --> 00:19:09,820
An object

227
00:19:11,180 --> 00:19:13,300
isn't as dangerous as the person holding it.

228
00:19:17,220 --> 00:19:17,900
Chris!

229
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:21,320
Chris, are you still there?

230
00:19:32,700 --> 00:19:33,700
Yes, Nadear?

231
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:35,260
You seem to be quick about this.

232
00:19:35,950 --> 00:19:37,100
Are you with Chris?

233
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:39,340
Yeah, I'm with Chris.

234
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:41,380
What are you two talking about?

235
00:19:42,660 --> 00:19:44,100
Just a normal conversation,

236
00:19:45,740 --> 00:19:46,500
nothing much.

237
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:52,040
I'll tell the waiters to come clean it up.

238
00:20:10,540 --> 00:20:11,180
Chris,

239
00:20:12,220 --> 00:20:13,320
come home. Now.

240
00:20:17,520 --> 00:20:18,780
This is obviously embezzlement.

241
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:20,080
How will you handle this?

242
00:20:22,260 --> 00:20:24,340
I told you, let me check it out first.

243
00:20:24,780 --> 00:20:26,200
Nan might have a reason

244
00:20:26,220 --> 00:20:28,100
for our expenses being higher than usual.

245
00:20:29,340 --> 00:20:31,100
No reason can justify this.

246
00:20:31,660 --> 00:20:33,840
What she did was wrong,
so she needs to be held accountable.

247
00:20:33,860 --> 00:20:34,700
Chris,

248
00:20:35,020 --> 00:20:37,340
Nan had been taking
care of our restaurant.

249
00:20:38,300 --> 00:20:39,180
Hey, Nadear,

250
00:20:39,420 --> 00:20:41,080
you can't use her good deeds
to justify her actions,

251
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:42,300
can you?

252
00:20:44,140 --> 00:20:46,980
Not everything is black and white
in our world, Chris.

253
00:20:48,300 --> 00:20:49,860
She might not want to do us wrong,

254
00:20:50,140 --> 00:20:51,780
but something forced her to.

255
00:20:52,940 --> 00:20:55,180
Why are you trying to make me
understand Nan?

256
00:20:55,980 --> 00:20:57,940
Shouldn't we discuss how to deal with this?

257
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:00,780
Why are you siding with Nan?

258
00:21:01,840 --> 00:21:02,860
D*mn it.

259
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:03,980
Chris!

260
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:09,240
It's because you never understood other people.

261
00:21:09,540 --> 00:21:11,300
Everything a person chooses to do,

262
00:21:11,860 --> 00:21:12,560
whether right or wrong,

263
00:21:12,580 --> 00:21:14,860
has a reason behind it.

264
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:16,340
It's because of money.

265
00:21:16,500 --> 00:21:17,880
She stole from us, Nadear.

266
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:19,600
Why do you think she did that then?!

267
00:21:19,620 --> 00:21:20,860
Have you ever thought about that?!

268
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:23,700
You never did, did you?

269
00:21:24,100 --> 00:21:26,420
Because you're obsessed
with always doing what's right.

270
00:21:27,060 --> 00:21:29,320
When are you going to learn
to understand other people?

271
00:21:34,780 --> 00:21:36,180
This is not working out for us.

272
00:21:37,420 --> 00:21:38,780
I don't understand you.

273
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:40,780
And you don't understand me.

274
00:21:42,300 --> 00:21:43,940
So why are we trying to fix this?

275
00:21:46,540 --> 00:21:47,740
Let's break up.

276
00:21:52,900 --> 00:21:54,440
You don't want to break up

277
00:21:55,280 --> 00:21:56,700
because we don't understand each other.

278
00:21:57,860 --> 00:21:59,380
But you want to break up

279
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:04,220
because you're so compatible
with that new friend of yours, right?

280
00:22:07,260 --> 00:22:08,860
What did she do

281
00:22:09,260 --> 00:22:10,360
to make you like her so much

282
00:22:10,380 --> 00:22:11,820
that you stayed with her all night?!

283
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:16,240
I can do

284
00:22:17,740 --> 00:22:19,260
what she did to you too.

285
00:22:39,980 --> 00:22:41,140
Stop it, Nadear.

286
00:22:41,580 --> 00:22:42,540
Please.

287
00:22:53,140 --> 00:22:54,800
How am I any different from her?

288
00:22:57,140 --> 00:22:59,040
Why can't it be me?

289
00:23:08,700 --> 00:23:10,340
The three months you asked me for

290
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:14,260
won't make our situation any better.

291
00:23:20,560 --> 00:23:22,020
Let's end it here.

292
00:24:17,140 --> 00:24:21,040
♫Trapped in a love that's a fading image♫

293
00:24:21,060 --> 00:24:24,820
♫Yet the love that never faded♫

294
00:24:24,840 --> 00:24:31,320
♫Like a missing page I can't find♫

295
00:24:31,340 --> 00:24:34,320
♫Your smell lingers vividly in my mind♫

296
00:24:34,340 --> 00:24:39,580
♫The touch from when you were by my side♫

297
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:42,420
Breaking up with her is
probably for the best.

298
00:24:44,820 --> 00:24:46,900
I'll tell her that I'm moving out.

299
00:24:48,860 --> 00:24:50,940
What about the three months
you promised her?

300
00:24:52,180 --> 00:24:54,740
If we keep this up,
it's just going to be toxic.

301
00:24:58,220 --> 00:25:00,220
Ever since I lost my memories...

302
00:25:02,860 --> 00:25:05,500
Love became nothing more than attachment.

303
00:25:08,260 --> 00:25:10,140
Even if it's three years,

304
00:25:11,900 --> 00:25:13,620
or thirty years,

305
00:25:15,960 --> 00:25:18,420
it still won't work out.

306
00:25:24,580 --> 00:25:26,840
I don't want you to be sad like this.

307
00:25:31,460 --> 00:25:34,100
I'm not sad because I had to break up with her.

308
00:25:35,780 --> 00:25:37,580
Ever since I lost my memories...

309
00:25:38,900 --> 00:25:41,340
Love was just attachment.

310
00:25:54,780 --> 00:25:56,420
I'm just sad that...

311
00:26:00,260 --> 00:26:02,060
our relationship ended badly.

312
00:26:03,340 --> 00:26:04,760
I'm sad that...

313
00:26:06,500 --> 00:26:08,700
the person who should
know me best

314
00:26:11,940 --> 00:26:13,940
doesn't understand me at all.

315
00:26:14,980 --> 00:26:17,220
If I didn't lose my memories,

316
00:26:18,340 --> 00:26:20,580
things might be a lot simpler.

317
00:26:24,640 --> 00:26:26,040
I'd be better off

318
00:26:26,060 --> 00:26:27,900
if I could remember everything.

319
00:26:54,420 --> 00:26:55,320
Chris!

320
00:26:58,060 --> 00:26:59,260
Keep it inside.

321
00:27:10,700 --> 00:27:11,300
Chris!

322
00:27:11,360 --> 00:27:12,060
Chris!

323
00:27:12,140 --> 00:27:12,940
Chris!

324
00:27:16,020 --> 00:27:17,540
You're in my room.

325
00:27:18,040 --> 00:27:19,220
It's okay.

326
00:27:21,420 --> 00:27:22,860
It was just a nightmare.

327
00:27:33,700 --> 00:27:34,500
Sun...

328
00:27:37,220 --> 00:27:38,540
you're alright now.

329
00:27:40,500 --> 00:27:41,780
I'm scared.

330
00:27:42,260 --> 00:27:43,660
I had a nightmare.

331
00:27:49,220 --> 00:27:50,060
Hm?

332
00:27:50,200 --> 00:27:51,740
Can you tell me about it?

333
00:28:09,260 --> 00:28:10,980
Which hand did you use
to touch the lock?

334
00:28:13,460 --> 00:28:14,540
My right hand.

335
00:28:25,080 --> 00:28:26,460
Where were you burned?

336
00:28:28,420 --> 00:28:29,300
Sun,

337
00:28:29,660 --> 00:28:31,060
it was a nightmare.

338
00:28:31,300 --> 00:28:32,780
How could I have an injury?

339
00:28:40,620 --> 00:28:41,540
Right here.

340
00:28:52,040 --> 00:28:53,520
When you add nice things

341
00:28:53,740 --> 00:28:56,020
to bad memories

342
00:28:57,060 --> 00:28:58,740
to create new memories,

343
00:28:59,360 --> 00:29:00,460
maybe...

344
00:29:00,700 --> 00:29:02,860
your trauma can heal faster that way.

345
00:29:17,180 --> 00:29:19,420
But when I was standing
in front of that door,

346
00:29:20,600 --> 00:29:21,940
I was so scared.

347
00:29:22,900 --> 00:29:24,800
I'm with you now.

348
00:29:25,580 --> 00:29:27,140
No matter where you are,

349
00:29:29,260 --> 00:29:30,820
if you have a nightmare again,

350
00:29:31,700 --> 00:29:33,660
remember this moment.

351
00:29:35,380 --> 00:29:36,980
I'll keep you company

352
00:29:38,240 --> 00:29:40,660
no matter what awaits
you on the other side of that door.

353
00:29:57,940 --> 00:29:59,180
Thank you, Sun.

354
00:30:01,660 --> 00:30:03,060
But I think I know

355
00:30:04,300 --> 00:30:06,340
what's waiting for me behind that door.

356
00:30:15,800 --> 00:30:17,380
Behind that door...

357
00:30:18,260 --> 00:30:19,320
are probably my memories

358
00:30:19,340 --> 00:30:21,160
of when I lost my parents.

359
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:26,100
It's probably because I'm scared
to face that memory,

360
00:30:27,640 --> 00:30:29,220
so it became a nightmare.

361
00:30:32,340 --> 00:30:34,420
What can you remember about your parents?

362
00:30:39,260 --> 00:30:41,340
I can only recall that it was very painful.

363
00:30:43,580 --> 00:30:44,900
I was devastated.

364
00:30:46,840 --> 00:30:48,680
But I can't remember the rest.

365
00:30:52,560 --> 00:30:53,820
I only have this photo

366
00:30:54,100 --> 00:30:55,820
to remind me of what
my parents looked like.

367
00:30:58,720 --> 00:31:00,740
Just thinking about looking
for other photos of them

368
00:31:00,760 --> 00:31:02,100
scares me.

369
00:31:03,860 --> 00:31:05,540
Ever since the accident,

370
00:31:07,740 --> 00:31:10,140
I couldn't even bring myself
to visit my parents' house.

371
00:31:17,940 --> 00:31:19,060
But if you run,

372
00:31:19,580 --> 00:31:20,780
you'll have to keep running.

373
00:31:23,820 --> 00:31:25,500
To overcome your fear,

374
00:31:26,820 --> 00:31:28,180
you'll have to face it.

375
00:31:31,100 --> 00:31:32,260
How?

376
00:31:36,520 --> 00:31:37,820
Find your memories.

377
00:31:58,740 --> 00:32:00,420
I'll stay by your side.

378
00:32:04,140 --> 00:32:07,230
[Third Person]

379
00:32:08,390 --> 00:32:12,240
[Third Person]

380
00:32:19,800 --> 00:32:21,230
I think it's here.

381
00:32:26,530 --> 00:32:27,230
Look!

382
00:32:27,430 --> 00:32:28,110
There are the horses!

383
00:32:28,230 --> 00:32:28,900
Let's go!

384
00:32:28,920 --> 00:32:29,830
Hey, wait...

385
00:32:31,010 --> 00:32:32,300
Do I have to ride the horse too?

386
00:32:32,920 --> 00:32:33,610
Don't be a chicken.

387
00:32:33,870 --> 00:32:36,530
You could do it when you were that tiny.

388
00:32:37,130 --> 00:32:38,020
Don't be scared.

389
00:32:39,430 --> 00:32:41,550
Who said I wasn't scared?

390
00:32:42,720 --> 00:32:44,670
I don't know how to ride a horse.
What if I fall off?

391
00:32:47,220 --> 00:32:49,390
You are in my hands now.

392
00:32:50,740 --> 00:32:52,260
No need to be afraid.

393
00:32:54,990 --> 00:32:55,550
Let's go.

394
00:32:57,460 --> 00:32:58,430
Excuse me!

395
00:32:58,720 --> 00:32:59,940
A horse, please!

396
00:33:00,650 --> 00:33:02,020
- Are you serious?
- Yes.

397
00:33:02,040 --> 00:33:02,390
Let's go.

398
00:33:04,390 --> 00:33:05,220
Is this a good idea?

399
00:33:10,350 --> 00:33:11,580
Look this way, please.

400
00:33:15,450 --> 00:33:16,740
You can go.

401
00:33:17,300 --> 00:33:19,280
Sun, didn't you say you'd go with me? Sun?!

402
00:33:19,550 --> 00:33:20,270
Bye-bye.

403
00:33:20,290 --> 00:33:21,000
Sun!

404
00:33:34,910 --> 00:33:36,510
Huh? How did you get here?

405
00:33:37,790 --> 00:33:39,960
Well, I promised to stay by your side.

406
00:33:40,920 --> 00:33:42,220
Thanks.

407
00:33:46,890 --> 00:33:47,730
Do you like it?

408
00:33:48,660 --> 00:33:49,530
Mm...

409
00:33:49,590 --> 00:33:50,990
But the horse is a bit tall.

410
00:34:16,310 --> 00:34:17,270
Are you tired?

411
00:34:20,600 --> 00:34:21,840
Do you remember anything?

412
00:34:24,870 --> 00:34:26,460
But I won't forget about today.

413
00:34:28,610 --> 00:34:30,020
Are you still scared?

414
00:34:33,380 --> 00:34:34,910
I'm not.

415
00:34:35,220 --> 00:34:37,110
It'd be much scarier
if you weren't here with me.

416
00:34:38,820 --> 00:34:41,350
Thank you for staying with me.

417
00:34:42,330 --> 00:34:43,620
You're like a talisman
that keeps ghosts away.

418
00:34:45,930 --> 00:34:46,910
You're crazy.

419
00:34:48,360 --> 00:34:49,620
Would you like to buy
handmade necklaces?

420
00:34:49,640 --> 00:34:50,520
Are you interested?

421
00:34:50,550 --> 00:34:52,510
Would you like one? I made them all myself.

422
00:34:53,440 --> 00:34:55,200
They're all so pretty. Are you interested?

423
00:35:01,070 --> 00:35:02,070
So cute.

424
00:35:02,520 --> 00:35:03,420
Pick one.

425
00:35:03,840 --> 00:35:05,110
I'll buy it for you

426
00:35:05,370 --> 00:35:07,220
as a reward for riding that horse.

427
00:35:08,630 --> 00:35:09,810
I won't refuse, then.

428
00:35:09,830 --> 00:35:10,830
Mm.

429
00:35:12,150 --> 00:35:13,830
They're all pretty.

430
00:35:16,250 --> 00:35:16,950
Whoa...

431
00:35:18,040 --> 00:35:19,350
I'll have this one.

432
00:35:20,070 --> 00:35:20,840
So cute.

433
00:35:21,440 --> 00:35:23,030
A bracelet.

434
00:35:24,630 --> 00:35:25,510
How much is it?

435
00:35:25,530 --> 00:35:26,740
One hundred baht.

436
00:35:27,380 --> 00:35:28,140
Thank you.

437
00:35:31,420 --> 00:35:32,220
Thank you.

438
00:35:33,990 --> 00:35:34,940
Isn't this cute?

439
00:35:42,140 --> 00:35:43,320
Open your eyes.

440
00:35:47,050 --> 00:35:48,950
I knew it was going to be a bracelet.

441
00:35:50,350 --> 00:35:52,140
You're not surprised at all?

442
00:35:53,340 --> 00:35:56,930
Well, around seventy percent
of the things you've gifted me

443
00:35:57,440 --> 00:35:59,240
were bracelets.

444
00:36:04,310 --> 00:36:06,290
Well, your wrist is beautiful.

445
00:36:07,150 --> 00:36:08,150
Especially...

446
00:36:10,490 --> 00:36:11,730
when you do "that."

447
00:36:14,900 --> 00:36:15,830
Hey.

448
00:36:17,140 --> 00:36:18,090
I'm glad

449
00:36:18,120 --> 00:36:19,720
you haven't changed.

450
00:36:21,030 --> 00:36:21,530
Here.

451
00:36:22,530 --> 00:36:23,430
Let me put it on for you.

452
00:36:51,050 --> 00:36:52,110
Sun...

453
00:36:53,920 --> 00:36:55,710
You've given me
a bracelet before, haven't you?

454
00:37:07,550 --> 00:37:08,230
Chris!

455
00:37:09,550 --> 00:37:10,630
Chris, what's wrong?

456
00:37:18,680 --> 00:37:19,710
Breathe slowly.

457
00:37:37,290 --> 00:37:40,860
Didn't you say things would be
better if I gave Chris her freedom?

458
00:37:41,640 --> 00:37:43,640
So why did she leave me?

459
00:37:46,240 --> 00:37:48,610
I'm not happy at all, Jeen.

460
00:37:50,710 --> 00:37:52,850
I want her back.

461
00:38:01,040 --> 00:38:02,440
Chris called.

462
00:38:06,280 --> 00:38:07,340
Jeen,

463
00:38:07,920 --> 00:38:10,650
can you convince Chris to come back to me?

464
00:38:24,980 --> 00:38:26,020
Hello, Chris.

465
00:38:26,300 --> 00:38:26,960
Hello.

466
00:38:27,420 --> 00:38:29,240
I want to open the door
to my memories.

467
00:38:30,070 --> 00:38:31,440
I want to know the truth.

468
00:38:32,660 --> 00:38:34,630
I want all of my memories back.

469
00:38:58,960 --> 00:38:59,930
Did you finish your call?

470
00:39:00,450 --> 00:39:01,450
Shall we go home?

471
00:39:06,340 --> 00:39:07,340
Thanks, Sun.

472
00:39:08,050 --> 00:39:09,830
I have to apologize

473
00:39:10,570 --> 00:39:12,220
for bringing you here

474
00:39:12,240 --> 00:39:13,850
and causing you to have a panic attack.

475
00:39:14,450 --> 00:39:15,680
Are you even more scared now?

476
00:39:16,840 --> 00:39:17,720
I am.

477
00:39:18,560 --> 00:39:21,270
But if I don't do anything,
nothing will change.

478
00:39:22,820 --> 00:39:25,840
Before, just thinking about
my parents scared me.

479
00:39:26,130 --> 00:39:27,930
But now that I'm here...

480
00:39:28,320 --> 00:39:30,270
I want to learn more about them.

481
00:39:32,540 --> 00:39:34,500
Even though things ended badly...

482
00:39:34,950 --> 00:39:38,110
that doesn't mean we didn't
have good memories together.

483
00:39:42,060 --> 00:39:43,290
I want to remember everything

484
00:39:43,840 --> 00:39:45,720
because of you, Sun.

485
00:39:47,830 --> 00:39:48,800
How about

486
00:39:49,120 --> 00:39:51,340
visiting your parents' house next trip?

487
00:39:53,960 --> 00:39:54,750
Yeah.

488
00:40:00,750 --> 00:40:02,020
Thank you so much.

489
00:40:07,940 --> 00:40:08,520
Hey.

490
00:40:09,810 --> 00:40:10,830
The heart pendant is gone.

491
00:40:17,750 --> 00:40:19,850
It might have fallen off when you
had a panic attack.

492
00:40:20,130 --> 00:40:22,230
It's alright. I'll buy you a new one.

493
00:40:23,240 --> 00:40:24,640
It's not the same, Sun.

494
00:40:30,620 --> 00:40:31,760
Are you in a rush?

495
00:40:33,140 --> 00:40:34,080
Why?

496
00:40:41,620 --> 00:40:43,270
[Do not litter on the beach]

497
00:40:49,810 --> 00:40:51,130
It has to be around here.

498
00:40:52,220 --> 00:40:53,220
Are you serious?

499
00:40:53,870 --> 00:40:55,140
It has to be.

500
00:40:55,350 --> 00:40:56,410
Where did it go?

501
00:41:14,630 --> 00:41:15,630
Your phone!

502
00:41:20,240 --> 00:41:21,960
Chris isn't answering my calls.

503
00:41:22,200 --> 00:41:24,620
Can you call her for me?

504
00:41:25,100 --> 00:41:28,020
Tell her to come get
urgent treatment or something.

505
00:41:29,390 --> 00:41:30,440
Calm down.

506
00:41:30,730 --> 00:41:32,940
Chris already said she
wants to remember everything.

507
00:41:33,320 --> 00:41:34,830
She'll be back.

508
00:41:34,850 --> 00:41:37,240
She'll come back after
she's already with someone else?

509
00:41:42,080 --> 00:41:43,160
Does she...

510
00:41:43,420 --> 00:41:44,940
love you right now, Nadear?

511
00:41:46,930 --> 00:41:48,900
If you're not going to help,

512
00:41:48,930 --> 00:41:50,270
don't say that to me.

513
00:41:50,730 --> 00:41:52,220
I'm saying the truth.

514
00:41:52,820 --> 00:41:54,230
Perhaps...

515
00:41:54,250 --> 00:41:56,180
it's time for you to admit...

516
00:41:56,200 --> 00:41:57,660
Don't stick your nose into this
if you're not helping!

517
00:41:59,050 --> 00:42:01,740
I'll make her mine again myself.

518
00:42:03,480 --> 00:42:04,240
Nadear.

519
00:42:05,230 --> 00:42:06,250
Excuse me!

520
00:42:06,270 --> 00:42:07,270
Hey!

521
00:42:08,240 --> 00:42:09,020
How much per bucket?

522
00:42:09,040 --> 00:42:09,880
One hundred each.

523
00:42:10,310 --> 00:42:11,530
Two purple buckets, please.

524
00:42:11,550 --> 00:42:12,320
Okay.

525
00:42:14,680 --> 00:42:16,030
Give me one pink bucket, please.

526
00:42:16,120 --> 00:42:17,340
Okay.

527
00:42:19,100 --> 00:42:21,130
Why are you doing it alone?
Let me join in too.

528
00:42:25,940 --> 00:42:27,430
The total is three hundred baht.

529
00:42:27,450 --> 00:42:28,820
- I'll scan to pay.
- Okay.

530
00:42:29,540 --> 00:42:30,300
Done.

531
00:42:30,320 --> 00:42:31,150
Thank you.

532
00:42:36,510 --> 00:42:38,610
[Third Person
Bar - Bistro]

533
00:42:43,740 --> 00:42:45,520
Keep your girlfriend in check,
why don't you?

534
00:42:45,750 --> 00:42:47,270
Don't let her bother me.

535
00:42:47,780 --> 00:42:48,880
Or else I'll tell her

536
00:42:49,320 --> 00:42:50,830
what you did.

537
00:42:59,350 --> 00:43:00,920
Please take this.

538
00:43:05,420 --> 00:43:07,320
That bottle is already expired.

539
00:43:15,910 --> 00:43:17,530
I can't find it.

540
00:43:18,450 --> 00:43:19,390
Sun,

541
00:43:19,410 --> 00:43:21,110
how could you lie there? It's dirty.

542
00:43:21,130 --> 00:43:21,920
Get up.

543
00:43:21,950 --> 00:43:22,540
Come on.

544
00:43:23,110 --> 00:43:24,430
Are you WHO or something?

545
00:43:24,790 --> 00:43:25,790
- Come here.
- Hey.

546
00:43:28,850 --> 00:43:30,950
It's okay if you can't find it.

547
00:43:30,970 --> 00:43:32,260
You don't have to feel bad about it.

548
00:43:32,930 --> 00:43:35,330
You didn't mean to lose it, did you?

549
00:43:36,330 --> 00:43:38,800
Well, I've already lost a lot in my life.

550
00:43:39,950 --> 00:43:41,640
Whether it's my memories,

551
00:43:42,320 --> 00:43:44,220
the people I knew,

552
00:43:45,840 --> 00:43:46,940
or even my parents.

553
00:43:49,220 --> 00:43:51,830
I don't want to lose
anything in my life ever again.

554
00:43:54,450 --> 00:43:55,820
If you mean me,

555
00:43:56,670 --> 00:43:57,980
I won't go anywhere.

556
00:44:00,950 --> 00:44:01,950
Really.

557
00:44:16,210 --> 00:44:16,870
Oh!

558
00:44:20,530 --> 00:44:21,530
Found it!

559
00:44:21,750 --> 00:44:22,750
Whoa!

560
00:44:23,530 --> 00:44:24,530
You're good at this.

561
00:44:24,890 --> 00:44:26,280
Oh, thank you so much.

562
00:44:27,330 --> 00:44:28,160
Are you happy?

563
00:44:28,180 --> 00:44:29,090
Mm.

564
00:44:29,130 --> 00:44:30,260
It's so hard to find.

565
00:44:30,970 --> 00:44:32,020
It's so small.

566
00:44:32,270 --> 00:44:33,900
- Thank you.
- I have good eyes.

567
00:44:33,930 --> 00:44:35,710
Well done.

568
00:44:36,890 --> 00:44:41,460
[Third Person]

569
00:44:42,650 --> 00:44:46,520
[Third Person]

570
00:44:59,510 --> 00:45:00,440
It's a shame, isn't it?

571
00:45:01,430 --> 00:45:03,320
We can't see the sunset from this beach.

572
00:45:05,570 --> 00:45:09,280
We could have made
more beautiful memories together.

573
00:45:12,020 --> 00:45:14,120
If we can't watch the sunset together,

574
00:45:15,640 --> 00:45:16,800
then...

575
00:45:22,610 --> 00:45:24,610
shall we watch the sunrise together?

576
00:45:35,190 --> 00:45:38,200
What's that photo? Delete it now.

577
00:45:39,020 --> 00:45:40,200
It's cute.

578
00:45:42,830 --> 00:45:43,600
Delete it.

579
00:45:43,620 --> 00:45:45,600
Hey, don't, Sun.

580
00:45:45,620 --> 00:45:48,080
I don't want to lose any photos.

581
00:45:48,900 --> 00:45:49,680
Fine.

582
00:45:50,240 --> 00:45:52,720
But if you don't have any space,
don't come back to erase it.

583
00:45:53,440 --> 00:45:54,170
Yes.

584
00:45:54,550 --> 00:45:55,250
Give it here.

585
00:45:59,940 --> 00:46:01,040
You have a tattoo?

586
00:46:07,480 --> 00:46:09,000
Mm.
[CN]

587
00:46:10,420 --> 00:46:11,860
I can't remember...

588
00:46:12,310 --> 00:46:14,000
where I got this from.

589
00:46:17,090 --> 00:46:19,640
You probably got it
because you loved her a lot.

590
00:46:30,640 --> 00:46:32,520
[Nadear]

591
00:46:43,080 --> 00:46:44,910
Can you answer my call?

592
00:46:44,940 --> 00:46:46,960
I want to talk about our restaurant.

593
00:46:49,120 --> 00:46:50,400
You can talk to her.

594
00:46:50,770 --> 00:46:51,800
I don't mind.

595
00:46:54,710 --> 00:46:55,710
I'll be back.

596
00:46:56,080 --> 00:46:57,160
One sec.

597
00:46:57,660 --> 00:46:58,240
Mm.

598
00:46:58,260 --> 00:46:59,220
I'll be quick.

599
00:47:03,540 --> 00:47:04,540
Yes, Nadear?

600
00:47:05,040 --> 00:47:06,200
Did something happen
at the restaurant?

601
00:47:07,090 --> 00:47:08,760
I missed you.

602
00:47:10,180 --> 00:47:12,060
It was my fault.

603
00:47:12,080 --> 00:47:13,600
I was rushing things.

604
00:47:14,800 --> 00:47:16,740
Can you come back to me?

605
00:47:17,520 --> 00:47:19,720
Didn't you want to talk about the restaurant?

606
00:47:20,230 --> 00:47:22,400
If it's not about our restaurant,

607
00:47:23,400 --> 00:47:25,320
would you talk to me?

608
00:47:27,120 --> 00:47:27,920
Nadear,

609
00:47:28,820 --> 00:47:31,520
whether I talk to you or not,
my feelings are the same.

610
00:47:32,090 --> 00:47:33,560
Let's not be together.

611
00:47:34,240 --> 00:47:36,020
It really isn't going to work out.

612
00:47:38,130 --> 00:47:40,440
Why don't we end this on a positive note?

613
00:47:41,410 --> 00:47:43,480
If you really want to end it here,

614
00:47:45,750 --> 00:47:47,680
I can't stop you.

615
00:47:49,940 --> 00:47:51,720
I still want to be your friend, though.

616
00:47:56,040 --> 00:47:57,240
I'll hang up now, Nadear.

617
00:48:07,340 --> 00:48:09,640
I can't be your friend, Chris.

618
00:48:29,330 --> 00:48:30,230
Excuse me,

619
00:48:30,810 --> 00:48:32,640
where did the woman at this table go?

620
00:48:32,900 --> 00:48:33,500
Oh,

621
00:48:33,520 --> 00:48:35,000
she seemed to have left.

622
00:48:35,310 --> 00:48:36,310
Huh?

623
00:48:43,180 --> 00:48:43,920
Sun!

624
00:48:45,660 --> 00:48:46,510
Sun!

625
00:48:49,520 --> 00:48:50,520
Sun!

626
00:48:52,400 --> 00:48:53,240
Chris!

627
00:49:01,980 --> 00:49:03,800
I thought you left me.

628
00:49:04,070 --> 00:49:05,700
I just went to get my power bank

629
00:49:06,340 --> 00:49:07,340
from the car.

630
00:49:07,360 --> 00:49:08,240
I also found...

631
00:49:08,360 --> 00:49:09,960
this sugar figurine.

632
00:49:11,350 --> 00:49:12,240
Isn't it cute?

633
00:49:13,510 --> 00:49:14,690
It's sweet too.

634
00:49:14,710 --> 00:49:16,030
Wanna try?

635
00:49:21,940 --> 00:49:23,120
You're so much sweeter.

636
00:49:25,810 --> 00:49:27,480
Can you not disappear like that again?

637
00:49:29,650 --> 00:49:31,160
If you don't want me to disappear,

638
00:49:31,550 --> 00:49:33,240
make me yours, then.

639
00:50:07,760 --> 00:50:10,280
You know I was just
teasing you earlier, right?

640
00:50:11,930 --> 00:50:13,880
Even if you're not mine,

641
00:50:14,830 --> 00:50:16,200
I won't leave you.

642
00:50:29,410 --> 00:50:31,880
I want to make great memories
with you here, Sun.

643
00:50:49,380 --> 00:50:51,440
A memory I'll never forget.

644
00:51:05,780 --> 00:51:07,810
I won't let you forget either.

645
00:51:26,560 --> 00:51:29,560
♫Every morning when I see the Sun,♫

646
00:51:29,580 --> 00:51:33,110
♫It reminds me of you, hun♫

647
00:51:33,130 --> 00:51:37,110
♫Your smile is always so bright♫

648
00:51:37,130 --> 00:51:40,840
♫The smile imprinted in my heart♫

649
00:51:42,100 --> 00:51:49,110
♫Lost in this hour of romantic reverie♫

650
00:51:49,130 --> 00:51:52,520
♫I wish time would stop for me♫

651
00:51:52,840 --> 00:51:57,250
♫To cherish this moment♫

652
00:51:58,570 --> 00:52:04,100
[CN]

653
00:52:04,900 --> 00:52:05,800
Sun.

654
00:52:06,470 --> 00:52:10,000
♫Always being near, hugging you tight,♫

655
00:52:11,110 --> 00:52:12,540
I love you, Chris.

656
00:52:14,490 --> 00:52:21,740
♫If you have to face the storm,
once the rain goes by♫

657
00:52:21,760 --> 00:52:23,640
I love you even more, Sun.

658
00:52:24,270 --> 00:52:28,120
♫The Sun will be there, shining in the sky♫

659
00:52:28,140 --> 00:52:32,600
♫'Cause I'm your SUN♫

660
00:52:34,710 --> 00:52:36,720
Can you do it for me?

661
00:52:38,540 --> 00:52:42,180
♫I'll be your sun, you'll be my sky,♫

662
00:52:42,210 --> 00:52:46,400
♫I'll kiss you tonight till the sun starts to rise♫

663
00:53:02,220 --> 00:53:09,140
♫Lost in this hour of romantic reverie♫

664
00:53:09,210 --> 00:53:12,240
♫Would time stop for me♫

665
00:53:12,880 --> 00:53:16,160
♫For all eternity?♫

666
00:53:16,190 --> 00:53:24,150
♫Let me be like the sunlight♫

667
00:53:24,180 --> 00:53:26,580
♫Providing warm embrace♫

668
00:53:26,600 --> 00:53:29,800
♫Always being near, hugging you tight,♫

669
00:53:29,820 --> 00:53:34,040
♫So you don't shed a tear♫

670
00:53:34,410 --> 00:53:42,500
♫If you have to face the storm, once the rain goes by♫

671
00:53:42,520 --> 00:53:44,420
♫When you look up high♫

672
00:53:44,440 --> 00:53:48,040
♫The Sun will be there, shining in the sky♫

673
00:53:48,090 --> 00:53:50,870
♫'Cause I'm your SUN♫

674
00:53:50,890 --> 00:53:54,440
♫I'll be your sun, you'll be my sky♫

675
00:53:54,520 --> 00:53:58,360
♫I'll be your sun, you'll be my sky♫

676
00:53:58,380 --> 00:54:00,360
♫When you look up high♫

677
00:54:00,380 --> 00:54:04,170
♫The Sun will be there, shining in the sky♫

678
00:54:04,190 --> 00:54:08,520
♫'Cause I'm your SUN♫

679
00:54:13,530 --> 00:54:15,240
This Sun is much prettier.

680
00:54:21,440 --> 00:54:22,960
Won't you look a bit more?

681
00:54:25,500 --> 00:54:27,550
I've been looking at you all night.

682
00:54:27,580 --> 00:54:28,880
Let me sleep some more.

683
00:54:45,920 --> 00:54:46,920
What are you doing?

684
00:54:47,580 --> 00:54:49,060
Leaving a mark on you,

685
00:54:49,410 --> 00:54:51,440
so people know that you're mine.

686
00:54:53,450 --> 00:54:56,080
I don't want our relationship
to be a secret anymore.

687
00:54:57,720 --> 00:54:58,070
[CN]

688
00:54:58,090 --> 00:54:59,390
Aren't you scared your father will find out?

689
00:55:00,910 --> 00:55:01,830
I am,

690
00:55:02,490 --> 00:55:04,560
but it's scarier if someone
steals you from me.

691
00:55:07,840 --> 00:55:09,500
No one can take me away

692
00:55:09,570 --> 00:55:10,800
if I don't want to go.

693
00:55:19,160 --> 00:55:20,900
[CN]

694
00:55:34,670 --> 00:55:35,400
Chris,

695
00:55:35,870 --> 00:55:37,200
shall we have breakfast?

696
00:55:45,030 --> 00:55:46,510
It's only been one night,

697
00:55:46,530 --> 00:55:47,790
and you want to get engaged?

698
00:55:47,810 --> 00:55:49,240
Aren't you a little too easy?

699
00:55:49,450 --> 00:55:51,020
I might be,

700
00:55:51,040 --> 00:55:52,440
but only for you, Sun.

701
00:55:52,460 --> 00:55:53,880
Chris doesn't love you.

702
00:55:54,010 --> 00:55:54,840
Chris loves...

703
00:55:54,880 --> 00:55:56,320
Don't you dare say her name!

704
00:55:56,450 --> 00:55:57,640
Don't eat that cake, Sun.

705
00:55:57,730 --> 00:55:59,440
- Nan, stop!
- Let go of me!

706
00:56:00,380 --> 00:56:01,160
Nadear.

707
00:56:01,360 --> 00:56:03,320
I really want us to be back together.

708
00:56:03,590 --> 00:56:04,510
Thank you

709
00:56:04,530 --> 00:56:06,570
for remembering I wanted to swim.

710
00:56:06,590 --> 00:56:07,600
Actually...

711
00:56:08,010 --> 00:56:09,620
I want to do something else as well.

712
00:56:23,440 --> 00:56:33,300
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

713
00:56:33,320 --> 00:56:38,440
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

714
00:56:38,460 --> 00:56:42,460
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

715
00:56:42,560 --> 00:56:48,560
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

716
00:56:48,580 --> 00:56:58,300
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

717
00:56:58,320 --> 00:57:03,360
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

718
00:57:03,380 --> 00:57:07,660
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

719
00:57:07,680 --> 00:57:16,320
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

720
00:57:16,840 --> 00:57:25,210
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫
